ology, H. Lee Moffitt Cancer Center and Research Institute, Tampa, Florida 33612, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Gillies RJ", "lastName": "Gillies", "firstName": "Robert J", "initials": "RJ", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-8888-7747"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Cancer Physiology, H. Lee Moffitt Cancer Center and Research Institute, Tampa, Florida 33612, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Schabath MB", "lastName": "Schabath", "firstName": "Matthew B", "initials": "MB", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-3241-3216"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Cancer Epidemiology, H. Lee Moffitt Cancer Center and Research Institute, Tampa, Florida 33612, USA."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-8888-7747"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-3241-3216"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "supporting_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "8", "volume": "11", "journalIssueId": 3211395, "dateOfPublication": "2021 Aug", "monthOfPublication": 8, "yearOfPublication": 2021, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Cold Spring Harb Perspect Med", "title": "Cold Spring Harbor perspectives in medicine", "essn": "2157-1422", "issn": "2157-1422", "isoabbreviation": "Cold Spring Harb Perspect Med", "nlmid": "101571139"}, "printPublicationDate": "2021-08-01"}, "pubYear": "2021", "pageInfo": "a039537", "abstractText": "Medical imaging is the standard-of-care for early detection, diagnosis, treatment planning, monitoring, and image-guided interventions of lung cancer patients. Most medical images are stored digitally in a standardized Digital Imaging and Communications in Medicine format that can be readily accessed and used for qualitative and quantitative analysis. Over the several last decades, medical images have been shown to contain complementary and interchangeable data orthogonal to other sources such as pathology, hematology, genomics, and/or proteomics. As such, \"radiomics\" has emerged as a field of research that involves the process of converting standard-of-care images into quantitative image-based data that can be merged with other data sources and subsequently analyzed using conventional biostatistics or artificial intelligence (AI) methods. As radiomic features capture biological and pathophysiological information, these quantitative radiomic features have shown to provide rapid and accurate noninvasive biomarkers for lung cancer risk prediction, diagnostics, prognosis, treatment response monitoring, and tumor biology. In this review, radiomics and emerging AI methods in lung cancer research are highlighted and discussed including advantages, challenges, and pitfalls.", "affiliation": "Department of Cancer Physiology, H. Lee Moffitt Cancer Center and Research Institute, Tampa, Florida 33612, USA.", "publicationStatus": "epublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["review-article", "Review", "Journal Article", "Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "U01 CA186145", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "U01 CA196405", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "U01 CA200464", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "U01 CA143062", "orderIn": 0}]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Humans"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Lung Neoplasms", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "DG", "qualifierName": "diagnostic imaging"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Diagnostic Imaging", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "TD", "qualifierName": "trends"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Artificial Intelligence"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Image Processing, Computer-Assisted"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Precision Medicine"}]}, "subsetList": {"subset": [{"code": "IM", "name": "Index Medicus"}]}, "fullTextUrlList": {"fullTextUrl": [{"availability": "Free", "availabilityCode": "F", "documentStyle": "pdf", "site": "Unpaywall", "url": "http://perspectivesinmedicine.cshlp.org/content/11/8/a039537.full.pdf"}, {"availability": "Free", "availabilityCode": "F", "documentStyle": "html", "site": "Unpaywall", "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8288444"}, {"availability": "Subscription required", "availabilityCode": "S", "documentStyle": "doi", "site": "DOI", "url": "https://doi.org/10.1101/cshperspect.a039537"}, {"availability": "Free", "availabilityCode": "F", "documentStyle": "html", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC8288444"}, {"availability": "Free", "availabilityCode": "F", "documentStyle": "pdf", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC8288444?pdf=render"}, {"availability": "Free", "availabilityCode": "F", "documentStyle": "doi", "site": "DOI", "url": "https://doi.org/10.1101/cshperspect.a039537"}]}, "isOpenAccess": "N", "inEPMC": "Y", "inPMC": "Y", "citedByCount": 97, "hasReferences": "Y", "hasTextMinedTerms": "Y", "hasDbCrossReferences": "N", "hasPDF": "Y", "hasBook": "N", "hasSuppl": "N", "hasLabsLinks": "Y", "hasData": "Y", "authMan": "Y", "epmcAuthMan": "N", "nihAuthMan": "Y", "manuscriptId": "NIHMS1691070", "hasTMAccessionNumbers": "Y", "tmAccessionTypeList": {"accessionType": ["doi"]}, "dateOfCompletion": "2021-12-17", "dateOfCreation": "2021-01-12", "dateOfRevision": "2023-08-01", "electronicPublicationDate": "2021-08-02", "firstPublicationDate": "2021-08-02", "firstIndexDate": "2021-01-13", "fullTextReceivedDate": "2025-02-04", "embargoDate": "2022-07-11", "hasEvaluations": "N"}]}}